<heading>connect - Connect to an existing box.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
connect NAME
connect NAME --direction north
connect NAME --world NLP
connect NAME --direction east --oneway
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Creates a connection from the current box to an existing box. Unlike dig,
connect does not create a new box. A connection is bidirectional by
default; use --oneway to make it traversable in one direction only.
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
The direction is the orientation at the current box, given as a compass
word or an angle in degrees (0° = the room's own east, counterclockwise).
Angles are relative to the room you stand in, never absolute compass
directions. The other side of the connection is its opposite angle.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
connect Kitchen
  Connect to an existing box called Kitchen.

connect Office --direction east
  Connect with the endpoint on the east side.

connect Wardrobe --world NLP
  Connect into a box of the NLP world.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
dig, enter, go, leave, look, refine split
</paragraph>
